    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Deletion targets" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs">MapWorkforceCollaborationEndpoints :133 → /api/v1/collab :142; the transitional group to remove.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Inert filter" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter.cs">:29 — superseded by CiamContactPrincipalStrategy, zero callers; delete.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check against teams-app-r1 for Api/ExternalAccess/** + Api/Filters/** before any edit; record the result.</step>
    <step order="2">Prove zero callers: grep ALL client surfaces (external-spa + every other client) and integration tests for /api/v1/collab and the workforce-collab endpoints; enumerate hits.</step>
    <step order="3">If ANY client still calls /api/v1/collab, STOP and invoke the escalation trigger — do not delete.</step>
    <step order="4">Delete ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter.cs (inert) and remove its DI registration/wiring.</step>
    <step order="5">Remove MapWorkforceCollaborationEndpoints, WorkforcePrincipalContextEndpoint, WorkforceCollaborationDownloadEndpoint, and WorkforceCallerAuthorizationFilter, plus the /api/v1/collab group mapping.</step>
    <step order="6">Remove/adjust the collab group's tests; ensure no orphaned references to the deleted types remain.</step>
    <step order="7">dotnet build + dotnet test — the full BFF suite must be green; confirm /api/v1/external routes are unaffected; no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="8">dotnet publish -c Release; record compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ANY client (grep across all client surfaces) still calls /api/v1/collab or the workforce-collab endpoints, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT delete the group until the caller is migrated.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish .NET</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell / grep</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/ (ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter + WorkforceCallerAuthorizationFilter deleted)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ (collab group + endpoints removed)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (collab tests removed/adjusted)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a repo-wide grep, when searching all client surfaces + tests for /api/v1/collab, then zero live callers exist BEFORE deletion (evidence recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter, WorkforceCallerAuthorizationFilter, MapWorkforceCollaborationEndpoints, WorkforcePrincipalContextEndpoint, and WorkforceCollaborationDownloadEndpoint no longer exist; the /api/v1/collab group is unmapped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The /api/v1/external ExternalCollaboration group + CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter are intact (no route regression).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full BFF suite is green with no orphaned references; no new HIGH CVE; publish ≤60 MB with delta vs 46.90 MB reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative gate: if a caller had been found, the deletion would NOT proceed (escalation fires).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    §10 BFF-touching deletion — Placement Justification + /conflict-check (teams-app-r1 shares this exact surface) +
